# Lines the language sweep in check-docs.sh may not flag.
#
# Format: <path>%%<substring>
# A hit is suppressed when its path matches an entry and the matched line
# contains that entry's substring.
#
# Every entry carries a comment saying why. An entry without a reason is a
# pattern that was weakened rather than a case that was understood.
#
# Do not widen an entry to cover a class of lines. If a whole file legitimately
# contains German, that file is either a verbatim quote of external output or a
# sign that the language-en module does not fit this project.

# --- The common false positives, present in most English repos --------------

# `die` — the shell error helper, and the English verb.
# `falls` — English "falls back / falls out of sync / falls through".
# `man` — the manual page.
# Add the specific lines here as they come up; there is no blanket entry,
# because a blanket entry stops the check from catching the real cases.

# --- Entries for this repo --------------------------------------------------

# The "Rolle" example is the language rule explaining itself: it names the
# translation layer it exists to prevent.
CLAUDE.md%%("Rolle" in the text

# "falls back" — the English verb, describing what `.buttonBorderShape(.circle)`
# does with a label that has no explicit square frame. The German `falls` is in
# the function-word list, which is why this one line needs naming.
CLAUDE.md%%the shape falls back to a
